WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.090
Time travel is complicated.

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:06.630
After all, if it was simple and straightforward,
then everyone would do it.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:12.039
Sure, on paper it sounds pretty easy to just
take a quick jaunt back to 1890, kill baby

00:00:12.039 --> 00:00:14.690
Adolf and avert World War Two.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:18.970
Millions of lives saved before lunch, and
surely the world would be all the better for

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:19.970
it, right?

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:25.890
But what if altering history didn’t change
the future - or the present as you knew it?

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:31.510
Perhaps instead, you unknowingly created a
new, alternate timeline, branching off from

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.829
the history you know into somewhere different?

00:00:34.829 --> 00:00:39.629
Maybe in this new timeline, where you traveled
back in time and killed Hitler, someone even

00:00:39.629 --> 00:00:44.399
worse rises to power and assumes control of
Germany before plunging the world into an

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:45.899
even deadlier war?

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:51.059
And even that is just one possible outcome
of your singular action, only fitting in with

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:55.909
one scientific theory of how the mechanics
of time travel might work, with no certainty

00:00:55.909 --> 00:00:58.670
that it actually would happen like that.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:03.160
Like we said, time travel is nowhere near
as easy as it seems in movies with flying

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.579
Deloreans and cyborg assassins who always
seem to keep coming back.

00:01:07.579 --> 00:01:12.270
Keeping all that in mind, these big, perplexing
questions about time travel and alternate

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.490
timelines is the perfect segue into the focus
of today’s video.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:21.420
Introducing SCP-1780, which is, brace yourselves...

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:22.939
A plastic name plate.

00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:26.930
You know, the official, business-like kind
that you might find displayed on a desk in

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:28.310
a fancy office.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:29.479
Wait, that’s it?

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:33.500
All that talk of world ending and the disruption
of multiple dimensional timelines is from

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.500
this thing?

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.909
You’re probably wondering what on infinite
earths this trivial piece of office stationery

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:43.170
could possibly have to do with the notion
of time travel, and we can tell you that the

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:46.299
connection will likely surprise you.

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:51.320
SCP-1780 itself appears pretty unassuming
at first, showing signs of aging and damage

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.039
from being buried for several decades.

00:01:54.039 --> 00:01:58.530
The first interesting detail of note, however,
is that name plates of the exact same style

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:04.570
were used in the offices of the SCP Foundation
itself, from the year 1990 all the way up

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.780
to as recently as 2003.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:12.040
SCP-1780 sports the Foundation’s emblem,
and the lettering on it is still legible despite

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.330
the wear and tear.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:18.870
While the name is redacted, the rest of it
reads: “Ph.D / Chairperson: Temporal Anomalies

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:19.870
Department”.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.590
Okay, so what could be so important about
a name plate?

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:26.530
Are the Foundation running so low on anomalies
that they have to lock up a harmless piece

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.320
of plastic from one of their very own offices?

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:30.320
Not quite.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:34.390
You see, you have already missed the second,
most interesting detail about this particular

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.680
name plate.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.030
Not only does the redacted name not match
any previous or existing staff member on their

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:46.140
database, but the SCP Foundation has never
even had a Temporal Anomalies Department.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.129
Not in this timeline, anyway.

00:02:48.129 --> 00:02:53.490
As for a “harmless name plate”, SCP-1780
is certainly anything but that.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:58.220
Of course, the name plate itself does remain
inactive if left alone, but when it is placed

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:04.660
into a mount of appropriate size, then…
well, it’s not exactly easy to explain what

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:09.890
happens, but we’ll try our best, seeing
as we’re “SCP Explained”, after all.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:16.020
Placing SCP-1780 into a name plate mount causes
a temporospatial anomaly to appear in the

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.610
nearest doorway.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:24.120
This anomaly is known as SCP-1780-1, and according
to high speed photographs taken by the SCP

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:30.099
Foundation, it appears instantly, so fast
that its speed can hardly be measured.

00:03:30.099 --> 00:03:34.519
Foundation researchers are flummoxed as to
exactly how this anomaly appears as well,

00:03:34.519 --> 00:03:38.299
unable to quantify what it is made from or
what forms it.

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:43.159
What they do know is that whatever space was
originally behind the doorway now containing

00:03:43.159 --> 00:03:48.590
SCP-1780-1 is now inaccessible through the
use of said door.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:53.430
However, whichever room was once behind the
doorway can still be accessed by going around

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:58.219
the door, either by destroying the adjacent
walls or using another entrance.

00:03:58.219 --> 00:04:04.329
The door that now contains SCP-1780-1 will
remain indestructible, and cannot be accessed

00:04:04.329 --> 00:04:07.879
while the SCP-1780 name plate is activated.

00:04:07.879 --> 00:04:14.630
So, SCP-1780-1, this temporospatial anomaly…
what exactly is it?

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:18.110
Once again, that is a question without an
easy answer.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:21.729
The best way to describe it would be to imagine
it as a portal.

00:04:21.729 --> 00:04:23.770
A portal leading where exactly?

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:30.160
Venturing through a doorway now hosting SCP-1780-1,
one will find themselves in an office.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:36.300
In fact, this office is an exact match to
one found inside the Euclid Objects Experimentation

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:41.740
Wing of Site 17, one of the SCP Foundation’s
top secret containment facilities where they

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.250
store a number of dangerous anomalies.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:50.710
The state of the SCP-1780-1 office varies
between visits, with signs of misuse, neglect

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.380
and general disrepair.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:56.419
However, the interior of this office always
contains the same items.

00:04:56.419 --> 00:05:00.930
Namely, there is standard office furniture,
the same type and style as those purchased

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:06.300
by the SCP Foundation during the renovation
of Site 17 in 1995.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:11.090
There are also a number of whiteboards around
the office, all with text and complex mathematical

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:12.889
equations written on them.

00:05:12.889 --> 00:05:18.830
The room also contains a loaded Remington
Model 870 shotgun, a copy of Oxford’s Unabridged

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:24.100
English Dictionary and three copies of Time
Life’s Great Ages of Man: A History of the

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:28.870
World’s Cultures, though strangely, only
one of these copies matches the history of

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.160
the world we know.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:36.880
Finally, there is another name plate inside
the office, a second instance of SCP-1780,

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.470
complete with a name plate bracket to hold
it.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:41.300
What does this all mean?

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:46.610
Is SCP-1780 capable of opening and closing
portals to just this single office?

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:51.380
And where or when is the SCP-1780-1 office?

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:52.850
Is it a pocket dimension?

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.940
A place in the future?

00:05:54.940 --> 00:06:00.640
According to tests run by the SCP Foundation,
the multiple SCP-1780 name plates can be used

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:05.330
to create several simultaneous SCP-1780-1
portals.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:09.830
Through the use of GPS tracking and other
redacted methods, the Foundation’s researchers

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:16.080
have been able to determine that, when there
are multiple instances of SCP-1780-1 doorways,

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.600
they will lead to the same office, in the
same physical space.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:25.040
However, the different portals will be separated
by an unknown interval of time.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:33.169
So, the leading theory is this: the office,
SCP-1780-1 is somehow temporally displaced.

00:06:33.169 --> 00:06:37.630
It does not exist within its proper place
in the linear timeline, and could instead

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.009
be located somewhere outside time.

00:06:41.009 --> 00:06:45.169
Anything left inside the office space, like
personal effects or even members of Foundation

00:06:45.169 --> 00:06:50.080
personnel that get left behind, will vanish
if the portal is closed and reopened.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:56.330
As long as the doorway remains open, SCP-1780-1
will behave in harmony with the normal flow

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.490
of time as we experience it.

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:04.610
But from the moment it closes, anyone left
inside the office is considered irretrievable.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.539
But that isn't all.

00:07:06.539 --> 00:07:12.569
Around one in every ten times that SCP-1780
is used to open the portal into the office,

00:07:12.569 --> 00:07:16.450
SCP-1780-1 will contain something else.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:20.080
Not just the items that usually appear in
the office, but people.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.660
Well, that might be a bit of a stretch.

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:26.480
They are humanoids, at least, shaped like
people.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:32.379
Referred to as SCP-1780-2, these entities
vary dramatically in their appearance and

00:07:32.379 --> 00:07:33.379
behavior.

00:07:33.379 --> 00:07:38.450
There is, nevertheless, one consistency to
them: they will all always claim to be personnel

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:41.400
working for the SCP Foundation.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:47.449
Some of the SCP-1780-2 have alleged themselves
to be Site 17 security staff, assigned to

00:07:47.449 --> 00:07:50.180
guard SCP-1780.

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:54.970
These entities are usually passive and cooperative
when existing Foundation security interacts

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:55.970
with them.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:08:00.169
Others have made the assertion that they are
field agents or researchers assigned to an

00:08:00.169 --> 00:08:02.039
unknown project.

00:08:02.039 --> 00:08:06.710
According to them, this project is focused
on dealing with temporal anomalies.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:13.820
These SCP-1780-2s tend to behave drastically
differently, and are often far more unpredictable.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:18.040
In some cases, they have even been hostile
towards Foundation personnel, and have even

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:21.400
self-terminated when efforts have been made
to contain them.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:28.280
The third and final type of SCP-1780-2 entity
seems to be singularly unique, even with its

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:33.270
own designation: SCP-1780-2a.

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:37.970
This entity refers to itself by the name Doctor
Thaddeus Xyank, and when questioned by the

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:41.350
Foundation, will refuse to give any information
at all.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:45.540
A number of times, personnel have asked this
Doctor Xyank about his origins, the goals

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:50.520
of his research, even where or when he came
from, and every time, he hasn’t told them

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.970
anything of use.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:58.410
SCP-1780-2a cannot be captured either, and
seems to have an in-depth firsthand knowledge

00:08:58.410 --> 00:08:59.790
of the Foundation.

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:04.140
He is able to predict all their containment
tactics for hostile humanoids, and has used

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:08.130
this foresight to evade any attempt to capture
him for further questioning.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:12.070
Right now, there are probably a million questions
popping into your head.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:16.380
Is the SCP-1780-1 office part of a branching
timeline?

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:20.880
Are the entities within Foundation agents
from an alternate history, trapped and displaced

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:21.880
in time?

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:24.220
Well, some of the answers we may never know.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:30.910
But some might be found in SCP-1780-3, the
name given to a document that has often also

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:35.540
been found within the SCP-1780-1 office space.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:42.500
Much like the rest of the furniture and stationery
inside SCP-1780-1, this document seems to

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:47.830
be from the SCP Foundation itself, printed
on their letterhead from around 1998.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:55.650
The author of this document appears to have
been SCP-1780-2a, Doctor Thaddeus Xyank himself.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:10:00.730
Somehow, either as an intentional booby trap
or as some sort of side effect from the temporal

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:06.590
displacement of the office, SCP-1780-3 has
anomalous properties on the reverse side of

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:07.730
the paper.

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:12.840
After being accidentally exposed to this effect,
a Foundation agent disappeared and was presumed

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:21.340
dead, only to reappear within the office space
fourteen years later as an instance of SCP-1780-2,

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:25.510
appearing to have not physically changed one
bit in all that time.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:29.200
As for the contents of the SCP-1780-3 document?

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:33.780
It appears to be an introductory letter and
orientation materials composed by Doctor Thaddeus

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:39.420
Xyank and intended for the special project
team investigating temporal anomalies.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:44.040
Anyone that reads the full document has suffered
the same fate as that other agent, disappearing

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.720
through unknown means.

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:50.150
However, the Foundation has kept a hard copy
of the document in storage, with the reverse

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:52.950
obscured to prevent its anomalous effect.

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:57.520
An excerpt of Doctor Xyank’s letter is also
kept on file, available to read to those who

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:59.920
hold adequate security clearance.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:06.050
In this letter, Doctor Xyank explains that
there are, in fact, multiple different timelines.

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:09.990
According to him, of all the timelines to
exist, many have their own version of the

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:13.050
SCP Foundation or another similar organization.

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:18.470
But, only a few of these other alternate Foundations
have a specific department dedicated to studying

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:20.360
time based anomalies.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:25.310
That is why there is no Temporal Anomalies
Department in the SCP Foundation as we know

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:26.310
it.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:31.860
It could be possible that Doctor Thaddeus
Xyank and all the other SCP-1780-2s are staff

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:37.030
from a different version of the Foundation,
that exists on a different timeline.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:41.770
The letter continues, as Doctor Xyank claims
that “everything you know about temporal

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:44.640
dynamics is fundamentally flawed.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:48.690
Despite what even I might tell you, Paradoxes
Do Exist.

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:53.960
Loosely defined, a temporal paradox is any
situation arising from an interruption in

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:58.710
an ordered sequence of events which requires
that two contradictory outcomes be held as

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:01.510
true by the universe simultaneously.”

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:06.540
That sounds awfully verbose and complicated,
but what he means is, a time paradox occurs

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:09.620
when something disrupts the flow of a timeline.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:14.190
This then effectively splits the timeline
into two streams, creating a pair of similar,

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:18.370
yet slightly different timelines that continue
to flow parallel with each other.

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:22.590
You see, we experience time as a single path,
a straight line.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:27.560
Now, imagine that path in front of you had
multiple other paths branching off of it.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:31.740
Whichever way you choose to walk, a different
choice means you might’ve ended up walking

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:36.710
on another branching path that is similar,
but will always be separate, distinct, and

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:37.730
different.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:42.810
Doctor Xyank then goes on to outline the mission
statement of his Temporal Anomalies Department.

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:47.250
Their goal is, in essence, to safeguard and
protect these various timelines.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:51.440
They hope to ensure that the events that led
to the existence of their department, their

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:57.370
version of the SCP Foundation and even humanity
as a whole, must always happen as recorded

00:12:57.370 --> 00:12:58.660
by history.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:05.350
From a base of operations that is temporally
isolated, existing outside time, Doctor Xyank

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:09.660
and the Temporal Anomalies Department intend
to keep the history of human civilization

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:14.140
consistent and prevent any and all possible
future threats that might bring about the

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:16.040
end of the world as we know it.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:19.880
So, there we have it, SCP-1780.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:24.860
An unassuming name plate that opens a portal
to an office outside of time itself.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:29.741
An office belonging to a Foundation department
that doesn’t exist in this timeline, but

00:13:29.741 --> 00:13:34.540
whose mission is to protect ours and every
other branching path of possibilities.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:38.400
Like we said before, time travel: it’s pretty
complicated.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:41.029
Now go check out “SCP-5000 Why?

00:13:41.029 --> 00:13:47.430
- The Full Story Compilation” and “SCP-5545
- Mysterious Tunnels in Antarctica - ABNORMALITY”

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:50.770
for more mind-bending anomalies from the SCP
Foundation!

